{
  "raw": {
    "https://careers.jcu.edu.au/jobs/senior-lecturer-general-practice-rural-medicine-townsville-qld-australia": {
      "title": "Senior Lecturer, General Practice & Rural Medicine",
      "description": "Senior Lecturer, General Practice & Rural Medicine - Townsville, QLD, Australia Current Opportunities Applicant Login My Profile Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Senior Lecturer, General Practice & Rural Medicine 495846 Townsville Academic Part time Closing on: Oct 19 2026 Add to favourites View favourites Position Description Academic Level C | 0.30 (10.875 hours per week) FTE | Townsville Shape the next generation of doctors and contribute to better health outcomes. Bring your general practice experience into an engaging academic environment. Make a meaningful difference to rural, remote and underserved communities. $137,166 - $157,465 + 17% super & great benefits (pro rata) James Cook University (JCU) is seeking an experienced medical practitioner to join the College of Medicine and Dentistry as Senior Lecturer, General Practice and Rural Medicine . This is an opportunity to combine your clinical expertise with teaching, research and student supervision while helping prepare future doctors to make a difference across northern Australia and beyond. About the role As Senior Lecturer, General Practice and Rural Medicine, you will contribute to the coordination and delivery of teaching within JCU’s Bachelor of Medicine, Bachelor of Surgery program, primarily across Years 1 to 3. Your teaching will focus on social and behavioural sciences, preventive medicine, global health, health promotion and research methods, with scope for the role to evolve according to your expertise and interests. You will also contribute to postgraduate teaching, student research supervision and collaborative research relevant to the strategic priorities of the College of Medicine and Dentistry. Key responsibilities Contribute to teaching, assessment and subject coordination in the Bachelor of Medicine, Bachelor of Surgery program. Deliver research methods education at undergraduate and postgraduate levels through face-to-face and online formats. Supervise undergraduate, postgraduate coursework, Honours and Higher Degree by Research students. Participate in research and contribute to the development of a collaborative research program. Support JCU’s commitment to reconciliation, sustainability and the University values. About you You are an experienced medical practitioner who is passionate about medical education and improving health outcomes in rural and remote communities. You will bring: Current registration as a medical practitioner in Australia. Fellowship of the Royal Australian College of General Practitioners, the Australian College of Rural and Remote Medicine, or an equivalent qualification. Extensive clinical experience, with a focus on general practice. Experience teaching within undergraduate medical education. An understanding of academic and clinical service delivery in rural and remote areas. Strong interpersonal and people management skills. A relevant record of research, publications or conference presentations, experience working in rural or remote communities, and a willingness to undertake further formal training in medical education will be highly regarded. Why work at JCU As Australia’s university for the Tropics, JCU provides a purpose-driven and collaborative environment where your expertise can make a meaningful contribution to medical education and healthcare outcomes across rural, regional and remote Australia. JCU’s College of Medicine and Dentistry is committed to strengthening healthcare across northern Australia and beyond through socially accountable education, research, partnerships, advocacy and leadership. JCU offers: 5 weeks annual leave plus leave loading, pro rata Flexible work arrangements Up to 12 months paid parental leave Salary packaging options Paid study leave and staff development programs Fitness Passport and health insurance discounts Free Employee Assistance Program, including coaching and counselling How to Apply Click the ‘Apply’ button, where you will be asked to complete an application form. Alternatively, apply directly through the JCU Careers page and: Complete the application form. Upload your current resume. Upload a cover letter outlining your relevant experience against the key requirements and how your skills and experience will support your success in the role. For enquiries about the role, please contact Associate Professor Haleagrahara Nagaraja on 4781 6370 or via email haleagrahara.nagaraja@jcu.edu.au . JCU celebrates diversity and is committed to providing a safe, inclusive and welcoming environment. We encourage applications from people of all backgrounds who meet the requirements of the role. Recommended for you Space Systems Coordinator Townsville Professional Coordinate accurate space systems, data and stakeholder services that support effective University space planning, utilisation and minor works decisions. Manager, Space and Minor Works Projects Townsville Professional Lead the strategic planning and delivery of space, workplace design and minor works projects that enhance JCU’s built environment and support safe, sustainable and effective outcomes. Student Scholarship and Loans Officer Townsville Professional Support student success through the administration of scholarships, bursaries, and financial assistance programs while delivering outstanding service and advice to students and stakeholders. Facebook Twitter LinkedIn © James Cook University 1995 to 2026 | Cookie Preferences Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device I do not accept I accept"
    },
    "https://careers.jcu.edu.au/jobs/space-systems-coordinator-townsville-qld-australia": {
      "title": "Space Systems Coordinator",
      "description": "Space Systems Coordinator - Townsville, QLD, Australia Current Opportunities Applicant Login My Profile Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Space Systems Coordinator 495841 Townsville Professional Full time Closing on: Nov 8 2026 Add to favourites View favourites Position Description James Cook University (JCU) is creating a brighter future for life in the Tropics and beyond, through education and research that makes a difference locally and globally. Are you an organised, analytical and customer-focused professional who enjoys turning complex information into practical outcomes? Join James Cook University as our Space Systems Coordinator and help strengthen the quality, accessibility and use of space and building information across the University. We now have an exciting opportunity for a skilled Space Systems Coordinator to join the Estate Directorate within the Services Division. Full-time opportunity | 36.25 hours per week | Full-time role. Townsville location | Travel between campuses may be required from time to time. HEWL 6: $90,821 - $98,369 plus up to 17% superannuation. ABOUT THE ROLE As Space Systems Coordinator, you will maintain accurate and accessible space, building and occupancy information across JCU's facilities and space management systems. You will coordinate data validation, system updates, desktop and on-site audits, and prepare reliable plans, reports and analysis to inform space allocation, utilisation, workplace planning and minor works decisions. Working closely with University stakeholders, you will provide responsive systems support, training and guidance, resolve complex data and workflow issues, coordinate requests and inspections, and identify practical improvements to systems, data and service processes. You will also help ensure records and activities meet relevant University requirements, building information standards and workplace health and safety obligations. WHAT YOU WILL BRING TO THE ROLE You will bring relevant qualifications and experience, together with demonstrated experience administering information, facilities, space management or comparable corporate systems. You will be confident maintaining data integrity, resolving complex system and data issues, and using sound judgement to manage competing priorities under general to broad direction. Strong analytical, problem-solving, written communication, consultation and customer service skills are essential, including the ability to prepare clear reports and guidance, deliver training and build productive relationships across organisational levels. Knowledge of data governance, records management and facilities compliance, and experience with CAD, GIS, building information modelling or space visualisation tools, will be highly regarded. WHY JCU JCU offers a dynamic and culturally diverse workplace where your ideas are valued, your professional growth is supported, and your work-life balance is respected. Working under the values of Authenticity , Excellence , Integrity , and Respect , we support and empower our people through the provisions of; A generous superannuation scheme with up to 17% employer contributions with UniSuper. 5 weeks of annual recreation leave plus leave loading. 15 days paid sick/carers leave per year. Up to 6 months paid parental leave. A range of flexible working options. Staff study assistance and paid study leave. Ongoing professional development support. Fitness Passport. Corporate discount on health insurance. Free Employee Assistance Program (coaching and counselling). Well-equipped modern facilities and contemporary workspaces with access to on-site childcare and medical services at our Townsville and Cairns’ campuses. HOW TO APPLY Are you ready to make a difference? Join us at JCU, where your future meets the tropics. Click the ‘apply’ button to be redirected to the JCU careers page , create an applicant account and follow the steps below: Complete the application form. Upload your current resume. Upload a cover letter outlining your relevant experience in relation to the key requirements of the role and how your skills and experience will ensure your success in the role. For any enquiries about the role, please contact Nathan Shepherd, Associate Director Planning and Capital Development at nathan.shepherd@jcu.edu.au ABOUT OUR PROCESS At JCU, we are committed to employing individuals who meet the requirements of the role and align with our values. All applicants will be contacted and advised of an outcome once the recruitment process is finalised. Please visit our Information Privacy Policy to understand how your information is collected, stored, accessed and used. James Cook University encourages people from all backgrounds who meet the role requirements to apply. We value and celebrate the diversity of our community and are committed to providing a safe, inclusive and welcoming learning and working environment. Recommended for you Manager, Space and Minor Works Projects Townsville Professional Lead the strategic planning and delivery of space, workplace design and minor works projects that enhance JCU’s built environment and support safe, sustainable and effective outcomes. Student Scholarship and Loans Officer Townsville Professional Support student success through the administration of scholarships, bursaries, and financial assistance programs while delivering outstanding service and advice to students and stakeholders. WHS Support Officer (Fire & Emergency) Townsville Professional Join JCU’s Work Health and Safety team and support fire safety, emergency preparedness and first aid across the University. You’ll coordinate evacuation activities, undertake inspections and provide practical safety advice. Facebook Twitter LinkedIn © James Cook University 1995 to 2026 | Cookie Preferences Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device I do not accept I accept"
    },
    "https://careers.jcu.edu.au/jobs/manager-space-and-minor-works-projects-townsville-qld-australia": {
      "title": "Manager, Space and Minor Works Projects",
      "description": "Manager, Space and Minor Works Projects - Townsville, QLD, Australia Current Opportunities Applicant Login My Profile Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Manager, Space and Minor Works Projects 495840 Townsville Professional Full time Closing on: Oct 18 2026 Add to favourites View favourites Position Description James Cook University (JCU) is creating a brighter future for life in the Tropics and beyond, through education and research that makes a difference locally and globally. Are you an experienced leader in space planning, workplace design and minor works delivery who is ready to shape the future of a complex-built environment? Join James Cook University (JCU) and lead a diverse portfolio that supports effective, safe and sustainable outcomes across the University. We now have an exciting opportunity for a dynamic and experienced Manager, Space and Minor Works Projects to join the Estate Directorate within the Services Division. Full-time opportunity | 36.25 hours per week | Full-time role. Townsville location | Travel between campuses may be required from time to time. HEWL 9: $130,115 - $137,625 plus up to 17% superannuation. ABOUT THE ROLE Reporting to the Associate Director, Planning and Capital Development, you will lead the effective utilisation and continuous improvement of JCU’s built environment through strategic space planning, workplace design and the delivery of minor works and refurbishment projects. You will oversee project prioritisation, scope, resources, budgets, procurement, contracts, contractors, governance and performance reporting, ensuring minor projects are delivered safely, on schedule, within approved budgets and to agreed quality standards. You will also provide expert advice to University stakeholders and lead a high-performing team focused on collaboration, accountability, innovation and service excellence. WHAT YOU WILL BRING TO THE ROLE You will bring a relevant degree and extensive experience leading diverse minor works, refurbishment, workplace design and space optimisation portfolios. Your background will include project planning, stakeholder engagement, risk management, procurement, contract administration, contractor management and the oversight of significant operational and project budgets. You will be a skilled people leader and communicator who can influence outcomes, build capability, manage competing priorities and apply strategic, analytical and sound problem-solving judgement in a complex organisational environment. WHY JCU JCU offers a dynamic and culturally diverse workplace where your ideas are valued, your professional growth is supported, and your work-life balance is respected. Working under the values of Authenticity , Excellence , Integrity , and Respect , we support and empower our people through the provisions of; A generous superannuation scheme with up to 17% employer contributions with UniSuper. 5 weeks of annual recreation leave plus leave loading. 15 days paid sick/carers leave per year. Up to 6 months paid parental leave. A range of flexible working options. Staff study assistance and paid study leave. Ongoing professional development support. Fitness Passport. Corporate discount on health insurance. Free Employee Assistance Program (coaching and counselling). Well-equipped modern facilities and contemporary workspaces with access to on-site childcare and medical services at our Townsville and Cairns’ campuses. HOW TO APPLY Are you ready to make a difference? Join us at JCU, where your future meets the tropics. Click the ‘apply’ button to be redirected to the JCU careers page , create an applicant account and follow the steps below: Complete the application form. Upload your current resume. Upload a cover letter outlining your relevant experience in relation to the key requirements of the role and how your skills and experience will ensure your success in the role. For any enquiries about the role, please contact Nathan Shepherd Associate Director Planning and Capital Development at nathan.shepherd@jcu.edu.au ABOUT OUR PROCESS At JCU, we are committed to employing individuals who meet the requirements of the role and align with our values. All applicants will be contacted and advised of an outcome once the recruitment process is finalised. Please visit our Information Privacy Policy to understand how your information is collected, stored, accessed and used. James Cook University encourages people from all backgrounds who meet the role requirements to apply. We value and celebrate the diversity of our community and are committed to providing a safe, inclusive and welcoming learning and working environment. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) 8b1210fa Last Name (required) 878a32a6 Email (required) 8e15c2d0 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended for you Space Systems Coordinator Townsville Professional Coordinate accurate space systems, data and stakeholder services that support effective University space planning, utilisation and minor works decisions. Student Scholarship and Loans Officer Townsville Professional Support student success through the administration of scholarships, bursaries, and financial assistance programs while delivering outstanding service and advice to students and stakeholders. WHS Support Officer (Fire & Emergency) Townsville Professional Join JCU’s Work Health and Safety team and support fire safety, emergency preparedness and first aid across the University. You’ll coordinate evacuation activities, undertake inspections and provide practical safety advice. Sign up for Job Alerts First Name (required) 951edcc9 Last Name (required) 57b7347f Email (required) aa6f6dda Job Alert ddc0b482 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Estate 