    "https://careers.jcu.edu.au/jobs/communications-and-candidate-engagement-coordinator-townsville-qld-australia": {
      "title": "Communications and Candidate Engagement Coordinator",
      "description": "Communications and Candidate Engagement Coordinator - Townsville, QLD, Australia Current Opportunities Applicant Login My Profile Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Communications and Candidate Engagement Coordinator 495872 Townsville Professional Full time Closing on: Nov 1 2026 Position Description James Cook University (JCU) is creating a brighter future for life in the Tropics and beyond, through education and research that makes a difference locally and globally. Join JCU's Graduate Research School and lead communications and engagement initiatives that support higher degree by research candidates. You'll shape digital content, coordinate the HDR Ambassador Program, build industry and alumni partnerships, and use data and feedback to enhance candidate experiences. This newly created position offers the opportunity to establish and embed programs that strengthen connection, engagement and support across JCU's graduate research community. Full-time, fixed-term opportunity | 36.25 hours per week Based at the Townsville Bebegu Yumba campus, Douglas HEWL 7: $99,878.44 - $110,446.52 per annum plus up to 17% superannuation ABOUT THE ROLE As the Communications and Candidate Engagement Coordinator, you will lead initiatives that enhance the higher degree by research (HDR) candidate experience across JCU. You will develop and deliver communications, oversee digital content and channels, and coordinate programs that keep candidates informed, connected and engaged throughout their research journey. Working collaboratively across the University and with external partners, you will grow mentoring, professional development and networking opportunities, including the HDR Ambassador Program. Using feedback and engagement data, you will evaluate outcomes, drive continuous improvement and help build a vibrant, inclusive and connected graduate research community. WHAT YOU WILL BRING TO THE ROLE You will bring demonstrated experience developing and delivering integrated communication and engagement strategies within a complex organisation, supported by strong written communication skills across web, digital, campaign and social media channels. You will have a sound understanding of contemporary communication practices, digital content governance and accessibility requirements, together with the ability to interpret and apply organisational policies and standards. You will be confident managing complex programs or projects independently, resolving varied challenges and finding practical ways to improve established approaches. Your strong interpersonal, consultation and negotiation skills will enable you to build trusted relationships and gain support from a wide range of internal and external stakeholders. You will also be comfortable using data, feedback and evaluation findings to assess effectiveness, shape priorities and make evidence-based recommendations. A commitment to equity, inclusion and creating a positive candidate experience will be central to your approach. WHY JCU JCU offers a dynamic and culturally diverse workplace where your ideas are valued, your professional growth is supported, and your work-life balance is respected. Working under the values of Authenticity , Excellence , Integrity , and Respect , we support and empower our people through the provisions of; A generous superannuation scheme with up to 17% employer contributions with UniSuper 5 weeks of annual recreation leave plus leave loading 15 days paid sick/carers leave per year Up to 6 months paid parental leave A range of flexible working options Staff study assistance and paid study leave Ongoing professional development support Fitness Passport Corporate discount on health insurance Free Employee Assistance Program (coaching and counselling) Well-equipped modern facilities and contemporary workspaces with access to on-site childcare and medical services at our Townsville campus HOW TO APPLY Are you ready to make a difference? Join us at JCU, where your future meets the tropics. Click the ‘apply’ button to be redirected to the JCU careers page , create an applicant account and follow the steps below: Complete the application form. Upload your current resume. Upload a cover letter outlining your relevant experience in relation to the key requirements of the role and how your skills and experience will ensure your success in the role. For any enquiries about the role, please contact Gabby Ryan at gabby.ryan@jcu.edu.au ABOUT OUR PROCESS At JCU, we are committed to employing individuals who meet the requirements of the role and align with our values. All applicants will be contacted and advised of an outcome once the recruitment process is finalised. Please visit our Information Privacy Policy to understand how your information is collected, stored, accessed and used. James Cook University encourages people from all backgrounds who meet the role requirements to apply. We value and celebrate the diversity of our community and are committed to providing a safe, inclusive and welcoming learning and working environment. Recommended for you Manager, Laboratory and Technical Services (Clinical and Simulated Learning) Townsville Professional, Technical Lead safe, compliant and high-quality laboratory and technical services across Medicine, Nursing and Midwifery, Dentistry, Rehabilitation and Health Sciences, optimising teams, specialised facilities, simulation environments and resources to support student learning and service outcomes across JCU. Educational Technology Designer Townsville Professional Join JCU's Graduate Research School and help shape the future of researcher development through innovative online learning. This is a 2-year fixed-term opportunity. Financial Services Officer - Procurement Townsville Professional Join JCU as a Financial Services Officer – Procurement and provide practical purchasing and transactional support across the University. Use your attention to detail, systems capability and customer service skills to process procurement activities, support staff and suppliers, and help maintain accurate financial information. Facebook Twitter LinkedIn © James Cook University 1995 to 2026 | Cookie Preferences Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device I do not accept I accept"
    },
    "https://careers.jcu.edu.au/jobs/educational-technology-designer-townsville-qld-australia": {
      "title": "Educational Technology Designer",
      "description": "Educational Technology Designer - Townsville, QLD, Australia Current Opportunities Applicant Login My Profile Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Educational Technology Designer 495859 Townsville Professional Full time Closing on: Nov 1 2026 Position Description James Cook University (JCU) is creating a brighter future for life in the Tropics and beyond, through education and research that makes a difference locally and globally. Join JCU's Graduate Research School on a 2-year fixed-term opportunity and help shape the future of researcher development. You'll design engaging online learning, collaborate with subject matter experts and apply emerging technologies to create accessible, high-quality professional development experiences that support HDR candidates and researchers across the University. Full-time, fixed-term opportunity | 36.25 hours per week Based at the Townsville Bebegu Yumba campus, Douglas HEWL 7: $99,878.44 - $110,446.52 per annum plus up to 17% superannuation ABOUT THE ROLE As the Educational Technology Designer , you will play a key role in enhancing research capability across JCU by creating engaging, accessible and scalable online professional development. You'll transform priority face-to-face offerings into high-quality digital learning experiences and help shape a contemporary professional development program that supports researchers and research students across the University. Working closely with academic and professional colleagues, subject matter experts and Colleges, you will design and maintain online learning modules, apply emerging technologies, and use learner insights to continuously improve outcomes. This is an opportunity to influence future learning design practices, support innovation in researcher development, and make a lasting impact across JCU WHAT YOU WILL BRING TO THE ROLE We are looking for a creative and collaborative learning design professional with qualifications and/or experience in instructional design, educational technology or a related field. You enjoy creating engaging online learning experiences and can confidently use learning management systems, authoring tools and multimedia technologies to develop accessible, high-quality learning resources. You have a talent for working with subject matter experts and translating complex concepts into clear, engaging and pedagogically sound learning experiences. With an understanding of the higher education environment and the needs of researchers and research students, you are committed to creating inclusive, accessible and equitable learning opportunities. You are comfortable exploring emerging technologies and can apply generative AI and other educational technologies in a responsible and ethical way. Coupled with strong analytical, organisational and problem-solving skills, you can manage competing priorities, establish effective processes and continuously improve learning outcomes and the overall learner experience. WHY JCU JCU offers a dynamic and culturally diverse workplace where your ideas are valued, your professional growth is supported, and your work-life balance is respected. Working under the values of Authenticity , Excellence , Integrity , and Respect , we support and empower our people through the provisions of; A generous superannuation scheme with up to 17% employer contributions with UniSuper 5 weeks of annual recreation leave plus leave loading 15 days paid sick/carers leave per year Up to 6 months paid parental leave A range of flexible working options Staff study assistance and paid study leave Ongoing professional development support Fitness Passport Corporate discount on health insurance Free Employee Assistance Program (coaching and counselling) Well-equipped modern facilities and contemporary workspaces with access to on-site childcare and medical services at our Townsville campus HOW TO APPLY Are you ready to make a difference? Join us at JCU, where your future meets the tropics. Click the ‘apply’ button to be redirected to the JCU careers page , create an applicant account and follow the steps below: Complete the application form. Upload your current resume. Upload a cover letter outlining your relevant experience in relation to the key requirements of the role and how your skills and experience will ensure your success in the role. For any enquiries about the role, please contact Gabby Ryan at gabby.ryan@jcu.edu.au ABOUT OUR PROCESS At JCU, we are committed to employing individuals who meet the requirements of the role and align with our values. All applicants will be contacted and advised of an outcome once the recruitment process is finalised. Please visit our Information Privacy Policy to understand how your information is collected, stored, accessed and used. James Cook University encourages people from all backgrounds who meet the role requirements to apply. We value and celebrate the diversity of our community and are committed to providing a safe, inclusive and welcoming learning and working environment. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) 3d3f3d1c Last Name (required) cd7d8555 Email (required) dec664dd Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended for you Manager, Laboratory and Technical Services (Clinical and Simulated Learning) Townsville Professional, Technical Lead safe, compliant and high-quality laboratory and technical services across Medicine, Nursing and Midwifery, Dentistry, Rehabilitation and Health Sciences, optimising teams, specialised facilities, simulation environments and resources to support student learning and service outcomes across JCU. Communications and Candidate Engagement Coordinator Townsville Professional Create meaningful connections across JCU's graduate research community. Lead communications, digital engagement, ambassador and partnership initiatives that improve the HDR candidate experience and expand access to development, mentoring and career opportunities. This is a 2-year fixed-term opportunity. Financial Services Officer - Procurement Townsville Professional Join JCU as a Financial Services Officer – Procurement and provide practical purchasing and transactional support across the University. Use your attention to detail, systems capability and customer service skills to process procurement activities, support staff and suppliers, and help maintain accurate financial information. Sign up for Job Alerts First Name (required) 9c49d9f5 Last Name (required) 76ac6fe6 Email (required) 76199b30 Job Alert f87b76ec Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Graduate Research School Graduate Research School Employment Type Full time Full time Locations Townsville, QLD, Australia Townsville, QLD, Australia Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Facebook Twitter LinkedIn © James Cook University 1995 to 2026 | Cookie Preferences Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device I do not accept I accept Please choose the location(s)"
