    "https://careers.jcu.edu.au/jobs/casual-hdr-program-support-officer-townsville-qld-australia": {
      "title": "Casual HDR Program Support Officer",
      "description": "Casual HDR Program Support Officer - Townsville, QLD, Australia Current Opportunities Applicant Login My Profile Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Casual HDR Program Support Officer 495720 Townsville Professional Casual Closing on: Oct 26 2026 Graduate Research School (Townsville) $52.04 - $59.02 per hour We’re seeking a motivated casual HDR Program Support Officer to assist with candidature administration, milestone tracking and high‑quality support for HDR candidates and supervisors. You’ll help manage key processes across admissions, enrolments, variations, examinations and completions, while providing responsive customer service and accurate record‑keeping This role suits someone with strong organisational skills, attention to detail, confidence using enterprise systems, and the ability to work both independently and as part of a busy team. This position is based in Townsville and requires on-campus attendance. Current JCU students are not eligible to apply. How to Apply and Contact Details Apply now and help us create a healthier, more sustainable future for the Tropics. Click the ‘Apply’ button or visit the JCU Careers Page and follow these steps: Complete the application form Upload your current resume For further information, contact Gabby Ryan via email gabby.ryan@jcu.edu.au JCU celebrates diversity and is committed to creating a safe, inclusive, and welcoming environment for all. We encourage applications from people of all backgrounds who meet the role requirements. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) b758f552 Last Name (required) 5333c179 Email (required) a74ad186 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended for you Manager, Laboratory and Technical Services (Clinical and Simulated Learning) Townsville Professional, Technical Lead safe, compliant and high-quality laboratory and technical services across Medicine, Nursing and Midwifery, Dentistry, Rehabilitation and Health Sciences, optimising teams, specialised facilities, simulation environments and resources to support student learning and service outcomes across JCU. Communications and Candidate Engagement Coordinator Townsville Professional Create meaningful connections across JCU's graduate research community. Lead communications, digital engagement, ambassador and partnership initiatives that improve the HDR candidate experience and expand access to development, mentoring and career opportunities. This is a 2-year fixed-term opportunity. Educational Technology Designer Townsville Professional Join JCU's Graduate Research School and help shape the future of researcher development through innovative online learning. This is a 2-year fixed-term opportunity. Sign up for Job Alerts First Name (required) f2024c75 Last Name (required) 0959427d Email (required) 4c8ea8d9 Job Alert 70ca9124 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Graduate Research School Graduate Research School Employment Type Casual Casual Locations Townsville, QLD, Australia Townsville, QLD, Australia Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Facebook Twitter LinkedIn © James Cook University 1995 to 2026 | Cookie Preferences Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device I do not accept I accept Please choose the location(s)"
